This covers the code and its documentation: scripts/, methods/, similarity/, tests/,
cluster/, config/, docs/ and the files at the root.


2. The data this project created: CC BY 4.0

The files under data/ and results/ were made by this project and are released under the Creative
Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/),
copyright (c) 2026 the authors of the lecture-slide-alignment-benchmark repository:

- data/splits/       the M3AV split into m3av_a and m3av_b
- data/selection/    the 60 tuning and 140 test lectures
- data/attributes/, data/categories/
                     the lecture attributes (length, images, tables, layout boxes,
                     discipline), their checks and the levels per attribute
- data/importance/   the importance labels (0/1/2) of the 18,315 test units, the second
                     labelling, the agreement tables and the check key and check labels
- data/tuning/, data/final/
                     the tuning and final-run tables (per lecture accuracy and cost) and
                     every method's predicted slide per unit
- data/similarity/   the similarity tables of the 60 tuning and 140 test lectures
- data/analysis/     the tables and figures of the analysis
- results/           the same tables as LaTeX and the figures as PDF
- data/llm_cache.sqlite3
                     the LLM answers of the runs

These files hold the corpora's lecture ids, numbers and labels, not their text or slides.
The true slide of each unit (the true_slide column of data/final/predictions/ and of the
importance labels) repeats the ground truth of the corpus the lecture comes from, so its
reuse also follows that corpus's terms (third part).


3. The corpora: not included, under their own licences

The transcripts, slides and ground truth of the four corpora are not in this repository.
scripts/download.py fetches them from their official sources at pinned versions into
data/raw/ (kept out of git), and the scripts prepare them from there. Each stays under
its own terms:

- M3AV (Chen et al., ACL 2024; huggingface.co/datasets/CHHHH/M3AV_v1.0): CC BY-NC-SA 4.0;
  the copyright of the videos stays with their owners.
- MaViLS (Anderer et al., Interspeech 2024; github.com/andererka/MaViLS): the repository
  carries an Apache-2.0 licence, which its README states for the code; most slide decks
  are from MIT OpenCourseWare (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0), and the remaining decks have no stated
  terms.
- MCD (github.com/meghamariamkm2002/MCD) and Slide-Highlight
  (github.com/meghamariamkm2002/Slide_Highlight): no licence is stated, and the talks come
  from SlidesLive, whose terms do not allow passing the content on. They may not be
  redistributed; for them this repository holds the lecture ids and the numbers and
  labels derived from them (attributes, importance labels, predictions, run tables,
  similarity tables), not their text or slides.
